# automatic translation
#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &i18n-pimdataexporter;"
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Backing up is an essential practice for all users. &i18n-pimdataexporter; is"
" a great tool for backing up or moving all of your settings and email to a "
"new installation. You also use &i18n-pimdataexporter; to import previous "
"backups."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export &kmail; "
"Data...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> through the message view window or "
"&i18n-pimdataexporter; can be run as a standalone application by running "
"&i18n-pimdataexporter; in the application launcher."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To perform a backup, <action>select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Back Up "
"Data...</guimenuitem></menuchoice></action>, it will prompt you to close all"
" kdepim applications. <warning><para>Make sure you close all windows, data "
"loss is possible if you don't.</para></warning> Once you have closed them, "
"click <guibutton>Yes</guibutton> to continue, or <guibutton>No</guibutton> "
"to cancel."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will be prompted to create a backup name, enter the name into the "
"<guilabel>File</guilabel> textbox, &eg; "
"<replaceable>mymailsettings</replaceable>. The default filetype it saves as "
"is <filename role=\"extension\">.zip</filename>."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next screen will allow you to select what you wish to backup, by default"
" everything is selected."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmail; Mails selection will only backup mails in your <quote>Local "
"Folders</quote>, it will backup &imap; settings and download messages upon "
"restore. If you have emails on a &imap; server you wish to be backed up, you"
" should use <ulink url=\"help:/akonadi_folderarchive_agent\">Folder Archive "
"Agent</ulink> to archive those emails to a local folder."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Selection Dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Selection Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Selection Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The final screen shows the log of the backup up process. You can close the "
"window once you have reviewed the log and verified your backup was "
"successful."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To restore your backup, select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Restore "
"Data...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> within &i18n-pimdataexporter;."
msgstr ""

# automatic translation
#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Archive "
"Information</guimenuitem></menuchoice> you can select a backup archive and "
"view its content."
msgstr ""

